Blanc 1.25.0 is a desktop browser application built with Electron 44.
This package stages only the upstream tracked application files named by its
release allowlist and its lockfile-pinned production dependencies in an ASAR
archive. The build controller uses the EmberBSD SDK host API and host Node.js
26.12.1. Node.js runs upstream tests, the upstream adblock seed generator, and
the pinned @electron/asar tool. The application uses the separately installed
Electron 44.9.3 package. The Electron NPM package and electron-builder are not
installed or run.

The wrapper selects Electron's packaged-app mode and leaves Chromium sandbox
settings unchanged. NetBSD self-updates are disabled because pkgsrc owns updates.
The installed CycloneDX SBOM records the lockfile-pinned NPM dependencies,
their archive hashes and declared license values, plus the external Electron
44.9.3 package. It records host Node.js and @electron/asar as build tools.
Upstream license and attribution files remain in the installed package. The
package is restricted because Blanc identity artwork and trademarks do not grant
permission to redistribute a modified build under the Blanc name.

NetBSD/aarch64 runtime acceptance remains pending the Electron 44.9.3 package
and installed application checks.
